# RE:START — A Bounce Back Game

A complete third-person 3D adventure set in Aster, a dead futuristic city. You are a
Restorer: reconnect the energy network, solve the district puzzles, and bring the
city back to life.

Built with three.js and procedural art/audio. No paid assets, no build step, no
npm install, no internet connection required to play.

---

## Play on Windows

1. Double-click **`Play RE-START.bat`**.
2. Your default browser opens the game at `http://127.0.0.1:8137/`.
3. Keep the small console window open while playing; close it to stop the server.

Chrome or Edge is recommended. The server is a plain PowerShell TCP server, so it
needs no admin rights and no installed runtime.

## Controls

| Action | Key |
| --- | --- |
| Move | `W` `A` `S` `D` |
| Look | Mouse (pointer lock, or click-drag if lock is blocked) |
| Run | `Shift` |
| Jump | `Space` |
| Interact | `E` |
| Insight Spark | `H` |
| Pause menu | `Esc` |
| Fullscreen | `F` |

The **main menu** offers New Game, Continue (enabled after a save), Settings and
Controls. Progress is saved automatically at checkpoints, district restorations,
mission completions, and every 25 seconds while playing.

## Hackathon edition — three missions

1. **Arrival Plaza** — meet RELAY, learn the controls, leap the barricade, activate the plaza terminal.
2. **Solar Walkway** — cross the maintenance route, repair three arrays, activate the inverter and power the district relay.
3. **The Restart Core** — reserve power brings the remaining relay lines online; reach the Core, activate it, and watch Aster return.

The hackathon route focuses on the strongest movement, repair, restoration and finale moments. The original Water Station and Overgrown Courtyard assets remain in the project for future expansion, but are not required in this short demo flow.

## Insight Sparks

When you struggle (falls, repeated wrong puzzle attempts, or a long time on one
objective), RELAY offers an **Insight Spark**. Press `H` for a specific hint plus a
temporary **Insight Surge**: a speed/jump boost and a mid-air bounce. Sparks never
remove completed progress, repaired panels, collected cells, or checkpoints.
Setbacks only add knowledge — that is the bounce-back theme in mechanical form.

## Restoration

Before restoration the city is grey, foggy and silent. Each completed district turns
on windows, street lamps and holograms, grows instanced vegetation, starts water and
particles, and shifts the sky, fog, sun and music toward a warm, living palette.
The finale restores the entire district with a cinematic flythrough.

## Project structure

```
index.html                 UI shell + importmap
css/style.css              HUD, menus, cinematic overlays
js/main.js                 game loop, missions, saving, ending
js/core/                   input, procedural audio, save, math + collision
js/player/                 character controller, animation, camera rig
js/world/                  procedural textures/materials, sky, city, vegetation, VFX
js/world/districts/        Plaza, Solar, Water, Garden, Core (+ relay pylon)
js/gameplay/               missions, Insight Sparks, interactables, pickups
js/ui/UI.js                HUD / menu / cinematic interface
vendor/                    three.js r160 + loaders & post-processing (MIT)
js/player/RestorerModel.js procedural Restorer character + procedural animation
server.ps1                 local static server (PowerShell, admin-free)
Play RE-START.bat          Windows launcher
```

## Performance

Quality presets (Settings → Graphics Quality) change render resolution, shadow map
size, MSAA and bloom. The city is merged per-material for a low draw-call count,
vegetation is instanced, and collision uses a coarse spatial grid.

## Assets & licences

- **three.js** r160 — MIT licence (`vendor/`).
- **The Restorer** — built procedurally from three.js primitives in
  `js/player/RestorerModel.js` (head, face, hair, jacket, chest core, backpack, belt,
  gloves, cargo trousers and boots), with idle/walk/run/jump animation generated in code.
  No external character model is required to play.
- **Everything else** — sky shader, PBR textures, city, props, vegetation, particles,
  music and sound effects are generated procedurally at runtime from code in this folder.
- No paid assets, subscriptions or external services are required.
